# Your scorecards. Ignored on purpose: they name real players, and a fork or a
# pull request would publish them. The folder itself is kept, along with the
# note explaining what goes in it, so a fresh clone still has somewhere to put
# the PDFs. `python3 tools/demo.py` also writes here, and its fictional season
# is likewise nothing to commit.
#
# If your club *wants* its cards in the repository -- a private repo, or results
# that are published anyway -- delete these four lines.
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep
!/data/README.md
!/data/*.md

# Your own config.toml, for the same reason as data/: [captains], [player_names]
# and [aliases] are lists of real people's names, and a fork or a pull request
# would publish them. `python3 build.py` writes this file for you from the cards,
# so a fresh clone is never without one for long. config.example.toml, which
# documents every setting and invents every name in it, is committed instead.
#
# Delete this line if you want your settings in the repository — a private repo,
# or a second machine to clone onto, are both good reasons.
/config.toml

# Generated dashboard. Rebuilt from data/ by `python3 build.py`, so it is not
# committed by default. Delete this line if you want the built site in git —
# publishing to GitHub Pages from the repo is a legitimate reason to.
/site/

# Design and development notes. Working documents, not part of the product.
/notes/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
